                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This VN made me metaphorically dizzy, the story is so twisted and just keeps spinning all the way until the end.\nI went in blind, with my only expectation being that it's some kind of horror/denpa, and while it does include these elements, the actual depth of the plot went vastly beyond my imagination. Although the mystery begins near instantly, the plot tends to feel rather slow at times during the first half in particular, however this VN is one of the rare cases where slice-of-life content didn't bore me too much overall, mostly due to the rotational narrative structure and silly quirks in the translation. \nEventually the plot develops into something extremely convoluted and intricate, encompassing a large variety of connections and abstract concepts, some of which I haven't even grasped probably. What starts as a time-loop story with psychological horror and shocking gore, evolves into manifold layers of various timelines and dimensions, and can be considered a commentary on philosophical concepts questioning the fundamental essence of being human (there's an unpredictable genre shift too but mentioning it feels too spoilery).\n\nI'd say that the heavy extend of complexity might be off-putting for many, as understanding the story requires high focus and structured thinking (both of which I don't possess lmao, I'm grateful to those who post explanations), and even then open questions and vague interpretations are likely to remain, but in my opinion the suspense and atmospheric presentation still keep it captivating despite confusion. I found it especially effective how the storytelling manages to induce uncertainty in the reader; the moment it feels like a reveal gets close, new mysteries pile up instead, towards the end I was too distrustful to even believe the final truths at first lol.\nAltogether I really enjoyed this experience, it was one of the most unpredictable VNs I've read! Above all it's remarkable how the story simultaneously offers a grounded, elaborate mystery, yet additionally serves as an abstract contemplation on complex philosophies.",
